+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396)
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "./src/index.js";
+
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: "e" } }, { a: "z", c: { d: null } }); // { a: "z", c: {} }
+```
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396, which obsoletes RFC 7386; the
+algorithm is the same) and returns the result as a new value; neither argument is mutated and the result
+shares no structure with them. An object patch merges member by member: `null` removes the member, any
+other value replaces or recursively merges it. A non-object patch (including an array or `null`) replaces
+the whole target. Notes: arrays are replaced, never merged; `null` cannot be set as a value; a non-object
+target is treated as `{}` when the patch is an object; `"__proto__"` and similar are ordinary keys. It
+never throws.
